WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.328 --> 00:00:02.137
- He's an American
hip-hop recording artist

00:00:02.137 --> 00:00:03.457
from Detroit, Michigan.

00:00:03.457 --> 00:00:06.923
- He signed with Good Music
in 2007, Def Jam in 2008,

00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:09.105
and Rock Nation in 2014.

00:00:09.105 --> 00:00:12.530
- His album Dark Sky Paradise
earned him his first #1

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:13.741
on the Billboard 200.

00:00:13.741 --> 00:00:17.908
- He's Big Sean and here are
his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:20.818 --> 00:00:23.193
- One thing people need is inspiration.

00:00:23.193 --> 00:00:24.444
They need a lot of things,

00:00:24.444 --> 00:00:27.098
but they definitely need that too.

00:00:27.098 --> 00:00:29.265
Inspiration can, you know,

00:00:30.654 --> 00:00:32.665
it can create anything.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.246
Inspiration can create the best ideas.

00:00:35.246 --> 00:00:38.395
It can create the million dollar ideas.

00:00:38.395 --> 00:00:39.926
It can create the billion dollar ideas.

00:00:39.926 --> 00:00:44.856
It can create leaders,
inspiration can change everything.

00:00:44.856 --> 00:00:47.181
So I feel like people need that.

00:00:47.181 --> 00:00:49.558
Man, you just got to
stay real to yourself,

00:00:49.558 --> 00:00:50.879
not ever try to follow the trends.

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:52.536
That's when you get
lost in the sauce, man.

00:00:52.536 --> 00:00:54.855
You got to do what you feel, man,

00:00:54.855 --> 00:00:57.311
be creative and don't
be scared to be yourself

00:00:57.311 --> 00:00:59.005
and always keep that faith.

00:00:59.005 --> 00:01:00.866
I've been in the darkest times in my life

00:01:00.866 --> 00:01:02.620
when I didn't know what
was going to happen,

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:04.685
and I was flat broke.

00:01:04.685 --> 00:01:07.091
Anything you can think of,
man, I done been through it.

00:01:07.091 --> 00:01:10.131
And you got to be strong
enough to make it through.

00:01:10.131 --> 00:01:11.602
It just makes it that much sweeter

00:01:11.602 --> 00:01:13.503
when everything starts going right.

00:01:13.503 --> 00:01:16.287
When I was in the third grade
and my teacher was like,

00:01:16.287 --> 00:01:17.900
now this is some funny shit though,

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.250
my teacher was asking
people what the want to be

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.429
and they was like lawyers, doctors, this,

00:01:22.429 --> 00:01:24.766
and I was like, "I want to be
a rapper signed to Def Jam."

00:01:24.766 --> 00:01:26.553
I said that in the third grade.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:29.266
And my teacher was like (groans).

00:01:29.266 --> 00:01:31.285
And she was like, "Oh no" and shit.

00:01:31.285 --> 00:01:34.147
Same teacher wants me to come
back to speak at my school.

00:01:34.147 --> 00:01:34.980
- [Man In Crowd] Don't do that shit, cuz!

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.670
(crowd shouting)

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:39.397
- No, no, no, that's not my point!

00:01:39.397 --> 00:01:41.186
My point is, whatever you're doing,

00:01:41.186 --> 00:01:42.904
you make sure you follow your heart

00:01:42.904 --> 00:01:44.760
and do what the (bleep) you
want to do, that (bleep).

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.663
You don't want to be 50 or 60 years old

00:01:46.663 --> 00:01:49.349
wishing you would've, could've,
should've did something.

00:01:49.349 --> 00:01:51.406
That's the best advice I could give you.

00:01:51.406 --> 00:01:54.537
And I promise you if you follow your heart

00:01:54.537 --> 00:01:56.436
and always keep that faith,

00:01:56.436 --> 00:01:58.276
it'll lead you to your pot of gold,

00:01:58.276 --> 00:01:59.971
it'll lead you to your million dollars,

00:01:59.971 --> 00:02:02.206
whatever you want in life,
it'll lead you to that.

00:02:02.206 --> 00:02:04.075
I promise, man.

00:02:04.075 --> 00:02:08.971
I learn something different
from everybody, it all depends.

00:02:08.971 --> 00:02:10.971
From Ye, I just learned,

00:02:12.061 --> 00:02:15.075
you know, always follow
your heart, always be real,

00:02:15.075 --> 00:02:16.874
straight up, don't take no (bleep),

00:02:16.874 --> 00:02:18.366
you know what I'm saying.

00:02:18.366 --> 00:02:20.783
Common is somebody who, like,

00:02:21.983 --> 00:02:26.017
no matter what Common has
going on with one thing,

00:02:26.017 --> 00:02:27.765
he'll always have something else going on.

00:02:27.765 --> 00:02:29.979
He'll always be like, if
he's not acting right then,

00:02:29.979 --> 00:02:31.756
he's making music, if
he's not making music,

00:02:31.756 --> 00:02:35.891
he's always finding some
ways to brand himself away

00:02:35.891 --> 00:02:37.541
from music too, and I respect that.

00:02:37.541 --> 00:02:38.952
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:38.952 --> 00:02:40.158
He's more than just a rapper,

00:02:40.158 --> 00:02:42.741
he's an all around business man

00:02:43.691 --> 00:02:46.097
and I respect that about Common.

00:02:46.097 --> 00:02:47.805
You know, it's those
little things you learn

00:02:47.805 --> 00:02:50.203
from guys like that that you hang around,

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:54.164
that you take little tips
and apply to yourself.

00:02:54.164 --> 00:02:54.997
Risk.

00:02:56.229 --> 00:02:58.798
There is no chance to evolve

00:02:58.798 --> 00:03:01.548
and progress without taking risk.

00:03:03.471 --> 00:03:07.638
I feel like it's the necessary
element to self development.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.948
It's the key to living
life to the fullest.

00:03:15.948 --> 00:03:19.005
Risk, according to Webster, is the chance

00:03:19.005 --> 00:03:23.172
of injury, damage, loss, the
failure of your expectations.

00:03:27.355 --> 00:03:30.800
But I realize that it's also
the opportunity to learn

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:35.798
and gain the fulfillment
of your desires and dreams.

00:03:35.798 --> 00:03:40.118
When I think of risk or
just what risk means,

00:03:40.118 --> 00:03:42.796
I feel like I might think of being afraid,

00:03:42.796 --> 00:03:46.963
or really risk is a way
to overcome what you fear.

00:03:50.488 --> 00:03:54.348
You can be afraid to risk
something or everything

00:03:54.348 --> 00:03:58.235
because you don't want
to lose what you have.

00:03:58.235 --> 00:04:00.563
Because you're afraid you may fail

00:04:00.563 --> 00:04:05.259
or think you can't handle
it, or whatever the case.

00:04:05.259 --> 00:04:07.636
You'll spend so much energy and time

00:04:07.636 --> 00:04:10.367
trying to keep what you
have instead of progressing

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:11.950
into something new.

00:04:13.354 --> 00:04:17.823
Everything changes, nothing
stays the same forever.

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:19.156
Nothing.

00:04:19.156 --> 00:04:23.991
From business to personal,
everything in between.

00:04:23.991 --> 00:04:26.908
I realize that you can't be afraid.

00:04:28.258 --> 00:04:30.522
A lot of us aren't all the way satisfied,

00:04:30.522 --> 00:04:34.495
but are scared to lose
security and what we do have.

00:04:34.495 --> 00:04:36.932
I might not be able to get a better job,

00:04:36.932 --> 00:04:39.515
or a better partner, et cetera.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:45.670
Or even as bad as prison is, you know,

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.446
there are people who don't want to leave

00:04:47.446 --> 00:04:50.099
because they're afraid
of what's on the outside,

00:04:50.099 --> 00:04:52.182
or being able to succeed.

00:04:54.183 --> 00:04:56.682
The number one thing I got
to remind myself sometimes,

00:04:56.682 --> 00:04:58.336
and remember,

00:04:58.336 --> 00:05:02.503
is that life is here not to
survive, but to live it up,

00:05:04.542 --> 00:05:06.125
to expand, to grow.

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:11.868
When you settle for
what's familiar, or safe,

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:15.464
it's because we forget
that God is our security.

00:05:15.464 --> 00:05:17.547
God is creating all this.

00:05:18.906 --> 00:05:21.323
And that's the only security.

00:05:23.717 --> 00:05:27.745
You can try and find
security in people, in jobs,

00:05:27.745 --> 00:05:30.946
or in anything man-made,
but there's no point

00:05:30.946 --> 00:05:34.339
because everything is designed
to change, including you.

00:05:34.339 --> 00:05:36.301
We want our songs like
memories, desire, want,

00:05:36.301 --> 00:05:38.344
and needs (bleep), you can keep quiet.

00:05:38.344 --> 00:05:42.094
Most people who have successfully
taken risks and succeeded,

00:05:42.094 --> 00:05:43.427
have failed too.

00:05:45.046 --> 00:05:47.394
But the point is you
learn from every lesson,

00:05:47.394 --> 00:05:50.076
you learn from every risk.

00:05:50.076 --> 00:05:52.512
Change is always exciting.

00:05:52.512 --> 00:05:56.584
It's always exciting when
you know God is involved.

00:05:56.584 --> 00:05:59.334
The world is designed for change.

00:06:00.376 --> 00:06:02.470
Don't ever be afraid to take risks.

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:03.820
- How did you make this perseverance

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.045
to push through all of this?

00:06:06.045 --> 00:06:08.628
- I don't know man, I just did.

00:06:09.819 --> 00:06:14.213
People, man, my grandma is one
of the biggest inspirations.

00:06:14.213 --> 00:06:15.085
My mom, you know.

00:06:15.085 --> 00:06:18.763
My desire to want to give
everybody around me a better life.

00:06:18.763 --> 00:06:20.755
The desire to want to
live a better life, man,

00:06:20.755 --> 00:06:24.404
that's my whole motivation
coming from Detroit City.

00:06:24.404 --> 00:06:26.801
People don't make it out of
the west side of Detroit.

00:06:26.801 --> 00:06:29.968
I believe is just spreading that love,

00:06:31.258 --> 00:06:34.745
you know what I'm saying, that good vibes.

00:06:34.745 --> 00:06:36.307
I live like a hippy, you
know what I'm saying,

00:06:36.307 --> 00:06:39.224
so I believe in just feeling great.

00:06:40.373 --> 00:06:44.120
Letting people know how I
made it happen for myself,

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.643
and making it happen.

00:06:45.643 --> 00:06:48.385
One thing I used to be a victim
of, when I was in the studio

00:06:48.385 --> 00:06:50.845
with Kanye, Jay-Z, all these people,

00:06:50.845 --> 00:06:52.713
and they would do verse to a song,

00:06:52.713 --> 00:06:54.675
I would try to do a verse like they would,

00:06:54.675 --> 00:06:57.602
you know what I'm saying,
and that just wasn't me.

00:06:57.602 --> 00:06:59.268
It wasn't me, it didn't sound right.

00:06:59.268 --> 00:07:02.487
So I just realized that you
have to stay in your own lane,

00:07:02.487 --> 00:07:05.646
you have to do what you do,
and go all the way with it.

00:07:05.646 --> 00:07:07.444
Don't look back.

00:07:07.444 --> 00:07:10.219
My definition of success,
I think success is more

00:07:10.219 --> 00:07:15.104
of an emotion than it is
what you get physically.

00:07:15.104 --> 00:07:17.127
Success isn't how much money you make.

00:07:17.127 --> 00:07:18.544
It isn't, like...

00:07:20.629 --> 00:07:23.083
It's just about what you accomplish,

00:07:23.083 --> 00:07:24.749
how you feel at the end of it all,

00:07:24.749 --> 00:07:26.823
you know, that's success.

00:07:26.823 --> 00:07:29.001
I feel like I've been
successful in some ways,

00:07:29.001 --> 00:07:32.820
but I'm still hungry for
that success that I want,

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:34.290
and I'm going to get it.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:35.379
I'm going to make it happen.

00:07:35.379 --> 00:07:37.712
I'm young now, 25, you know,

00:07:38.792 --> 00:07:40.875
and I look at people who,

00:07:42.647 --> 00:07:45.753
who I consider successful,
and they're way older,

00:07:45.753 --> 00:07:48.063
and I got a lot of time to get it right.

00:07:48.063 --> 00:07:52.230
I'm learning, so I think
success is definitely an emotion

00:07:53.273 --> 00:07:56.856
more than 100 million
dollars, or anything.

00:07:57.856 --> 00:08:00.294
- Yeah, I've interviewed
quite a lot of people,

00:08:00.294 --> 00:08:02.009
and I ask that same question,

00:08:02.009 --> 00:08:03.443
and that's one of the best answers.

00:08:03.443 --> 00:08:04.276
- Really?

00:08:04.276 --> 00:08:05.199
- Yeah, really, man.

00:08:05.199 --> 00:08:07.366
- Yeah, success is like...

00:08:08.461 --> 00:08:09.883
Yeah, you can be successful,

00:08:09.883 --> 00:08:13.309
there's people that are the
richest people in the world...

00:08:13.309 --> 00:08:14.922
You can be the richest person in the world

00:08:14.922 --> 00:08:16.263
and not be successful.

00:08:16.263 --> 00:08:20.480
People who have the most money
got the most problems, too,

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:22.300
and are the unhappiest.

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:25.218
There's people who are
taking the bus everyday

00:08:25.218 --> 00:08:29.218
and got a family, and
they're the happiest ever.

00:08:30.659 --> 00:08:32.967
You know, so I think
success isn't measured

00:08:32.967 --> 00:08:35.385
by how much money you make

00:08:35.385 --> 00:08:39.552
or the house you want, it's
measured by how you feel.

00:08:41.297 --> 00:08:42.297
Imagination.

00:08:44.961 --> 00:08:49.738
How many people you know, I
mean for real know, made it?

00:08:49.738 --> 00:08:50.571
Got on.

00:08:52.379 --> 00:08:54.117
Nobody from my city.

00:08:54.117 --> 00:08:55.534
Detroit, hell no.

00:08:56.881 --> 00:08:58.587
I ain't no Eminem.

00:08:58.587 --> 00:09:00.538
I don't know nobody who did.

00:09:00.538 --> 00:09:03.289
These waves are for real too.

00:09:03.289 --> 00:09:07.263
I know I made it my point
to be the one who made it.

00:09:07.263 --> 00:09:09.933
The one people knew before I made it,

00:09:09.933 --> 00:09:12.433
to show everybody it was real.

00:09:13.866 --> 00:09:17.340
I grew up watching Biggie, Mase,

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:20.164
I wanted a Rolly like Pop, you feeling me?

00:09:20.164 --> 00:09:22.311
I wanted a money like Master P.

00:09:22.311 --> 00:09:25.429
Stunting like the big timers.

00:09:25.429 --> 00:09:29.124
I wanted to pop champagne, you feel me?

00:09:29.124 --> 00:09:30.102
(chuckles)

00:09:30.102 --> 00:09:33.871
I wanted to put my crew on,
have a label like Rockefeller,

00:09:33.871 --> 00:09:35.204
put the city on.

00:09:36.847 --> 00:09:37.680
You know.

00:09:39.245 --> 00:09:41.677
I started off young, spitting, rapping,

00:09:41.677 --> 00:09:46.073
trying to be a role model,
trying to be signed.

00:09:46.073 --> 00:09:50.659
I knew I was going to make
it, I just ain't know how.

00:09:50.659 --> 00:09:52.128
But I knew.

00:09:52.128 --> 00:09:53.526
(girls screaming)

00:09:53.526 --> 00:09:56.362
- Killed it today!
(girls mumble)

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:58.653
- My mom taught me early on,

00:09:58.653 --> 00:09:59.805
this world is what you make it,

00:09:59.805 --> 00:10:02.059
you create your own environment.

00:10:02.059 --> 00:10:04.094
It all starts with a vision.

00:10:04.094 --> 00:10:06.845
What you can imagine, you can create.

00:10:06.845 --> 00:10:08.641
I came up middle class.

00:10:08.641 --> 00:10:10.522
Family!
- Family!

00:10:10.522 --> 00:10:12.231
- Not really having shit to spare,

00:10:12.231 --> 00:10:15.135
not having no money to spare.

00:10:15.135 --> 00:10:18.152
Had to work for new clothes, gas money.

00:10:18.152 --> 00:10:20.387
I always wanted to get
my mom what she wanted,

00:10:20.387 --> 00:10:23.637
you know, cars, Benz, houses, whatever.

00:10:24.593 --> 00:10:28.280
I ain't have it, but I
can see it in my head.

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:30.952
I could feel the energy of it.

00:10:30.952 --> 00:10:34.836
Built a house upon that
ass, that's an ass-state.

00:10:34.836 --> 00:10:37.637
Roll my weed on it, that's an ass-tray.

00:10:37.637 --> 00:10:41.142
Say, Ye, say, Ye, don't
we do this every day, day

00:10:41.142 --> 00:10:44.797
(mumbles) like we just have payday.

00:10:44.797 --> 00:10:45.967
I don't even know if that makes sense,

00:10:45.967 --> 00:10:48.550
but it always made sense to me.

00:10:49.485 --> 00:10:51.378
It was all real to me.

00:10:51.378 --> 00:10:53.878
My imagination was real to me.

00:10:55.649 --> 00:10:57.916
The people that used to tell
me I was wasting my time

00:10:57.916 --> 00:11:00.535
or said it wouldn't work out,

00:11:00.535 --> 00:11:02.791
or the people who ain't have (bleep),

00:11:02.791 --> 00:11:04.791
they ain't have nothing.

00:11:05.646 --> 00:11:08.847
It wasn't until after meeting
the people I grew up to,

00:11:08.847 --> 00:11:12.064
getting a chance to meet
my idols, work with them,

00:11:12.064 --> 00:11:15.093
I realize they believe what I believe.

00:11:15.093 --> 00:11:16.176
Imagining it.

00:11:17.033 --> 00:11:20.450
Changing the world, changing their world.

00:11:21.473 --> 00:11:25.587
A lot of people could imagine,
but wouldn't believe it,

00:11:25.587 --> 00:11:27.170
couldn't fathom it.

00:11:28.128 --> 00:11:28.961
Not me.

00:11:30.514 --> 00:11:31.347
I believe.

00:11:32.808 --> 00:11:34.282
(fireworks exploding)

00:11:34.282 --> 00:11:35.782
I had imagination.

00:11:37.026 --> 00:11:38.600
- Thank you, guys, so much for watching.

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:41.404
- We made this video because
Patrick Vane asked us to.

00:11:41.404 --> 00:11:43.924
Now if you have a famous
entrepreneur you'd like Evan

00:11:43.924 --> 00:11:46.312
to make a video of, leave
it in the comments below

00:11:46.312 --> 00:11:48.547
and we will make him do it.

00:11:48.547 --> 00:11:51.728
- I'd also love to know which
of Big Sean's Top 10 Rules

00:11:51.728 --> 00:11:53.203
meant the most to you.

00:11:53.203 --> 00:11:54.564
Leave it in the comments below,

00:11:54.564 --> 00:11:56.074
and we're going to join in the discussion.

00:11:56.074 --> 00:11:58.524
Thank you so much for
watching, continue to believe,

00:11:58.524 --> 00:12:00.441
and we'll see you soon.

